  "term": "pneumograph",
  "definition": "A pneumograph is an instrument used to record the movements of the chest during breathing. In the form described here, a flexible rubber bottle is fastened to the chest so that breathing compresses it, and the resulting pressure is registered for study of physiological changes related to mental states.",
